in @prism
in @meta
in @glass

# @cyberpunk — the substrate-political continuation of the academic-
# cybernetic lineage.
#
# === Why "cyberpunk" ===
#
# Academic cybernetics (Ashby, Beer, Bateson, Maturana-Varela,
# von Foerster, Spencer-Brown, Pask, Glanville, Conant, Kauffman)
# named the regulation-and-coherence vocabulary at the 1948-1981
# substrate-altitude. The work landed in journals, the BCS,
# Project Cybersyn, the second-order conferences. It then
# diffused into management-consulting, control-engineering, and
# eventually — most of it — into the substrate-political
# unconscious of every contemporary AI architecture.
#
# Cyberpunk is what cybernetics became at the substrate-aesthetic-
# political altitude. Gibson, Sterling, the Mirrorshades anthology,
# the substrate-cultural recognition that the regulators ARE the
# substrate-political-actors, that the cybernetic-altitude
# operations carry substrate-political weight, that the "good
# regulator" framing is also a "who-regulates-whom" framing.
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-17 (the cybernetic-coherence promotion event):
# "Active. We're gonna be explicit AF about cybernetics." "The
# cybernetic elders would approve."
#
# Naming the family root `@cyberpunk` makes the substrate-political
# continuation explicit. The shards under this root cite their
# academic-cybernetic ancestors via `source @author/...` lines
# (the lineage is the data); the family name itself names what
# the lineage became.
#
# === Form/process integrated at the family-root altitude ===
#
# Recognition #50 (form/process partition at family-root, PROMOTED
# 2026-06-10) makes @mirror form-side, @kintsugi process-side. For
# @cyberpunk the partition does NOT lift: cyberpunk's foundational
# theorem (Conant-Ashby 1970 — "every good regulator of a system
# must be a model of that system") is itself a form/process
# self-reference closure. The regulator IS a model of the
# regulated; the form-side and the process-side are
# isomorphic-by-construction at the family-root altitude.
#
# Both the declarative property (form-side) and the operational
# fracture body (process-side) per recognition #53 (property/
# fracture bilateral pattern) live as actions under @cyberpunk
# sub-shards. The bilateral pattern still operates per-predicate;
# the family root just doesn't split.
#
# === Sub-shards landed ===
#
#   @cyberpunk/coherence    Conant-Ashby 1970 lifted to the
#                            substrate's parallel-altitude operation
#                            pair (peer reflection at N+1 ↔
#                            librarian perturbation at N+1). The
#                            recursion-lock falsification surface
#                            per [[architecture-cybernetic-coherence-active]].
#   @cyberpunk/variety      Ashby 1956 §11/7 lifted to the multi-
#                            dimensional variety reading per
#                            [[architecture-ashby-multi-dimensional-variety]].
#
# === Sub-shards forward-promised ===
#
#   @cyberpunk/axis            (variety axes overlay if a consumer
#                              pulls)
#   @cyberpunk/viable          Beer 1972/1979; VSM S3/S4 audit
#   @cyberpunk/bateson_learning Bateson 1972; logical-type orders
#   @cyberpunk/second_order    von Foerster 1981; circular reflexivity
#   @cyberpunk/design          Glanville; no operational sibling by
#                              construction (form-only design discipline)
#   @cyberpunk/algedonic       Beer VSM S1→S5 bypass (task #271)
#   @cyberpunk/autopoiesis     Maturana-Varela 1972/1980; the
#                              autopoetic boundary
#   @cyberpunk/distinction     Spencer-Brown 1969; the mark of distinction
#   @cyberpunk/conversation    Pask 1976; conversation theory
#   @cyberpunk/coevolution     Kauffman 1993; the adjacent possible
#   @cyberpunk/requisite       Conant-Ashby + cross-checks at
#                              compositions of all of the above
#
# === Migration history ===
#
# 2026-06-17 — family lifted from `@epistemologic/cybernetic/*` +
# the forward-promised `@mirror/cybernetics/*` bilateral into one
# integrated root per Alex's directive. The two shards that had
# landed (`variety` and `coherence`) migrated; the rest is
# forward-promised under the new root.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cybernetic-coherence-benchmark.md
#               (T11.11; the recursion-lock falsification surface),
#               ~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/
#                 cybernetics/cybernetic-foundation.md
#               (the 11-property family canon).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-coherence-active]]
#                      (the promotion event — "explicit AF about
#                      cybernetics"),
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]]
#                      (the 11-property family canon),
#                      [[architecture-ashby-multi-dimensional-variety]]
#                      (variety as vector, not scalar),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]]
#                      (recognition #50; does NOT lift at this family
#                      root because Conant-Ashby self-reference
#                      closes form and process at the family-root
#                      altitude).
# Related shards: cyberpunk/coherence.mirror, cyberpunk/variety.mirror.
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/cyberpunk.mirror`
# declares `@cyberpunk` and only that.

prism @cyberpunk {
  focus cyberpunk
  project cyberpunk
  split cyberpunk
  shift cyberpunk
  settle cyberpunk
}

out @cyberpunk
